  <object class="pygubu.builder.widgets.dialog" id="helpDialog">
    <property name="height">600</property>
    <property name="maxsize">600|600</property>
    <property name="minsize">600|600</property>
    <property name="resizable">none</property>
    <property name="width">600</property>
    <child>
      <object class="pygubu.builder.widgets.tkinterscrolledtext" id="helpText">
        <property name="padx">10</property>
        <property name="pady">10</property>
        <property name="state">disabled</property>
        <property name="text" translatable="yes">Program Documentation
=========================================================
INPUT
=========================================================
Select PDF Directory:

Click the ellipsis icon to select a directory containing your corpus of PDF documents. All documents of the filetype ".pdf" will be selected for analysis.
=========================================================
Select Keyword File:

Click the ellipsis icon to select your text file containing keywords of interest. The keyword file should be of the filetype ".txt" and contain each keyword on a new line. For example:

	Morphogenesis
	Blood-brain barrier
	Central nervous system
	Endothelial

You may also enter your keywords into the text box below, following the same format as above.
=========================================================
OUTPUT
=========================================================
Context Paragraph Length:

This number will change the number of words in the generated context paragraph. Defaults to 30 words.
=========================================================
Basic Letter/Number Filter:

Ticking this box will disable user filters and filter out anything that isn't a letter, number, or space. Should not be used if any keywords contain characters such as hyphens, as they will be caught by the basic filter.
=========================================================
Select Filter File:

Click the ellipsis icon to select your filter file containing characters to filter. The filter file should be of the filetype ".txt" and contain each filter character on a new line. For example:

	!
	@
	#
	©

You may also enter your filter characters into the text box below, following the same format as above.
=========================================================
Select Output Directory:

Click the ellipsis icon to select the directory where the output files will be saved.</property>
